# Phase 4 — ViewModel Passes Questions into the Submission

## Objective
Wire the actual questions the user saw into the submission at submit time.

## Main issue being solved
Without this, `submission.questions` is always empty for new submissions, so Phases 2–3 would always hit the (buggy) fallback.

## Proposed solution
`shared/.../presentation/tat/TATTestViewModel.kt`, in `submitTest()`:
```kotlin
val submission = TATSubmission(
    userId = userId,
    testId = state.testId,
    stories = state.responses,
    questions = state.questions,   // NEW — the exact set the user saw
    totalTimeTakenMinutes = totalTimeTakenMinutes,
    submittedAt = Clock.System.now().toEpochMilliseconds(),
    analysisStatus = AnalysisStatus.PENDING_ANALYSIS,
    olqResult = null
)
```

The ViewModel already holds `state.questions` — the exact set loaded by `loadTATTest`.

## Architecture rationale
- The ViewModel is the SSOT for the in-memory test session; it's the only place that knows the exact questions shown.
- No repository or use-case change needed — `SubmitTATTestUseCase` is a thin pass-through.

